\mt1 2 Timothy
\c 1
\s1 Paul’s Greeting to Timothy
\r (\ref 1 Timothy 1:1–2|1TI 1:1-2\ref*)
\p \v 1 Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus by \add the\add* will of God, according to \add the\add* promise of life in Christ Jesus,
\p \v 2 To Timothy, \add my\add* beloved child:
\p Grace, mercy, \add and\add* peace from God \add the\add* Father and Christ Jesus our Lord.
\s1 Faithfulness under Persecution
\r (\ref Matthew 10:16–25|MAT 10:16-25\ref*)
\p \v 3 I thank God, whom I serve with a clear conscience as did \add my\add* forefathers, as I constantly remember you night and day in my prayers. \v 4 Recalling your tears, I long to see you so that I may be filled with joy.
\p \v 5 I am reminded of your sincere faith, which first dwelt in your grandmother Lois and your mother Eunice, and I am convinced \add is\add* in you as well.
\p \v 6 For this reason I remind you to fan into flame the gift of God, which is in you through the laying on of my hands. \v 7 For God \add has\add* not given us a spirit of fear,\f + \fr 1:7 \ft Or \fqa timidity \ft or \fqa cowardice\f* but of power, love, and self-control.
\p \v 8 So do not be ashamed of the testimony of our Lord, \add or\add* of me, His prisoner. Instead, join me in suffering for the gospel by \add the\add* power of God. \v 9 \add He\add* has saved us and called \add us\add* to a holy calling, not because of our works, but by His own purpose and \add by the\add* grace He granted us in Christ Jesus before time began.\f + \fr 1:9 \ft Literally \fqa before times eternal\f* \v 10 And now He has revealed \add this grace\add* through the appearing of our Savior, Christ Jesus, \add who\add* has abolished death and illuminated the way to life and immortality through the gospel, \v 11 to which I was appointed \add as\add* a preacher, an apostle, and a teacher.
\p \v 12 For this reason, even \add though\add* I suffer \add as I do\add*, I am not ashamed; for I know whom I have believed, and I am convinced that He is able to guard what I have entrusted \add to Him\add*\f + \fr 1:12 \ft Or \fqa what He has entrusted to me\f* for that day.
\s1 Holding to Sound Teaching
\p \v 13 Hold on \add to the\add* pattern of sound teaching\f + \fr 1:13 \ft Literally \fqa sound words\f* you have heard from me, with \add the\add* faith and love that \add are\add* in Christ Jesus. \v 14 Guard the treasure entrusted \add to you\add*,\f + \fr 1:14 \ft Or \fqa the good deposit entrusted to you\f* with the help of \add the\add* Holy Spirit who dwells in us.
\p \v 15 You know that everyone in \add the province of\add* Asia\f + \fr 1:15 \ft Literally \fqa in Asia\ft ; Asia was a Roman province in what is now western Turkey. \f* has deserted me, including Phygelus and Hermogenes.
\p \v 16 \add May\add* the Lord grant mercy to the household of Onesiphorus, because he has often refreshed me and was unashamed of my chains. \v 17 Indeed, when he arrived in Rome, he searched diligently \add until\add* he found me.
\p \v 18 \add May\add* the Lord grant \add Onesiphorus His\add* mercy on that day. You know very well how much he ministered \add to me\add* in Ephesus.
\c 2
\s1 Grace and Perseverance
\r (\ref Hebrews 12:1–3|HEB 12:1-3\ref*)
\p \v 1 You therefore, my child, be strong in the grace that \add is\add* in Christ Jesus. \v 2 And the things that you have heard me \add say\add* among many witnesses, entrust these to faithful men who will be qualified to teach others as well.
\p \v 3 Join me in suffering, like \add a\add* good soldier of Christ Jesus. \v 4 A soldier refrains from entangling himself in \add civilian\add* affairs, in order to please the \add one who\add* enlisted him. \v 5 Likewise, a competitor does not receive the crown unless he competes according to the rules. \v 6 The hardworking farmer should be the first to partake of the crops. \v 7 Consider what I am saying, for the Lord will give you insight into all things.
\p \v 8 Remember Jesus Christ, raised from \add the\add* dead, descended from David, as proclaimed by my gospel, \v 9 for which I suffer to the extent of being chained like a criminal. But the word of God cannot be chained! \v 10 For this reason I endure all things for the sake of the elect, so that they too may obtain \add the\add* salvation that \add is\add* in Christ Jesus, with eternal glory.
\p \v 11 \add This is a\add* trustworthy saying:
\b 
\q1 If we died \add with Him\add*,
\q2 we will also live \add with Him\add*;
\q1 \v 12 if we endure,
\q2 we will also reign \add with Him\add*;
\q1 if we deny \add Him\add*,
\q2 He will also deny us;
\q1 \v 13 if we are faithless,
\q2 He remains faithful,
\q2 for He cannot deny Himself.
\s1 The Lord’s Approved Workman
\p \v 14 Remind  \add the believers \add* of these things, charging \add them\add* before God\f + \fr 2:14 \ft SBL, BYZ, and TR \fqa the Lord\f* to avoid quarreling over words, \add which\add* succeeds only in \add leading\add* the listeners to ruin.
\p \v 15 Make every effort to present yourself approved to God, \add an\add* unashamed workman who accurately handles the word of truth.
\p \v 16 But avoid irreverent, empty chatter, \add which\add* will \add only\add* lead to more ungodliness, \v 17 and the talk of \add such men\add* will spread like gangrene. Among \add them\add* are Hymenaeus and Philetus, \v 18 who have deviated from the truth. They say that the resurrection has already occurred, and they undermine the faith of some.
\p \v 19 Nevertheless, God’s firm foundation stands, bearing this seal: “\add The\add* Lord knows those who are His,”\f + \fr 2:19 \ref Numbers 16:5|NUM 16:5\ref* (see also LXX)\f* and, “Everyone who calls on the name of the Lord must turn away from iniquity.”
\p \v 20 A large house contains not only vessels of gold and silver, but also of wood and clay. Some indeed \add are\add* for honorable \add use\add*, but others \add are\add* for common \add use\add*. \v 21 So if anyone cleanses himself of \add what is unfit\add*,\f + \fr 2:21 \ft Literally \fqa cleanses himself of these\f* he will be a vessel for honor: sanctified, useful to the Master, \add and\add* prepared for every good work.
\p \v 22 Flee from youthful passions and pursue righteousness, faith, love, \add and\add* peace, together with those who call on the Lord out of a pure heart.
\p \v 23 But reject foolish and ignorant speculation, for you know that it breeds quarreling. \v 24 And a servant of \add the\add* Lord must not be quarrelsome, but must be kind to everyone, able to teach, \add and\add* forbearing. \v 25 \add He must\add* gently reprove those who oppose \add him\add*, in the hope that God may grant them repentance leading to a knowledge of \add the\add* truth. \v 26 Then they will come to their senses \add and escape\add* the snare of the devil, \add who\add* has taken them captive to his will.
\c 3
\s1 Evil in the Last Days
\p \v 1 But understand this: In \add the\add* last days terrible times will come. \v 2 For men will be lovers of themselves, lovers of money, boastful, arrogant, abusive, disobedient to \add their\add* parents, ungrateful, unholy, \v 3 unloving, unforgiving, slanderous, without self-control, brutal, without love of good, \v 4 traitorous, reckless, conceited, lovers of pleasure rather than lovers of God, \v 5 having a form of godliness but denying its power. Turn away from \add such\add* as these!
\p \v 6 They are the kind who worm their way into households and captivate vulnerable women \add who are\add* weighed down with sins \add and\add* led astray by various passions, \v 7 \add who are\add* always learning \add but\add* never able to come to a knowledge of \add the\add* truth.
\p \v 8 Just as Jannes and Jambres opposed Moses,\f + \fr 3:8 \ft See Jasher 79:27. \fqa The Book of Jashar \ft or \fqa the Book of the Upright One \ft is often cited as \fqa Jasher\ft .\f* so also these men oppose the truth. They are depraved in mind \add and\add* disqualified from the faith. \v 9 But they will not advance much further. For just like \add Jannes and Jambres\add*, their folly will be plain to everyone.
\s1 All Scripture Is God-Breathed
\r (\ref Hebrews 4:12–16|HEB 4:12-16\ref*)
\p \v 10 You, however, have observed my teaching, \add my\add* conduct, \add my\add* purpose, \add my\add* faith, \add my\add* patience, \add my\add* love, \add my\add* perseverance, \v 11 \add my\add* persecutions, \add and the\add* sufferings that came upon me in Antioch, Iconium, \add and\add* Lystra. What persecutions I endured! Yet the Lord rescued me from all \add of them\add*. \v 12 Indeed, all who desire to live godly \add lives\add* in Christ Jesus will be persecuted, \v 13 while evil men and imposters go \add from bad\add* to worse, deceiving and being deceived.
\p \v 14 But \add as for\add* you, continue in the things you have learned and firmly believed, since you know from whom you have learned \add them\add*. \v 15 From infancy you have known the Holy Scriptures, which are able to make you wise for salvation through faith in Christ Jesus. \v 16 All Scripture \add is\add* God-breathed and is useful for instruction, for conviction, for correction, \add and\add* for training in righteousness, \v 17 so that the man of God may be complete, fully equipped for every good work.
\c 4
\s1 Preach the Word
\p \v 1 I charge \add you\add* in the presence of God and of Christ Jesus, who will judge \add the\add* living and \add the\add* dead, and \add in view\add* of His appearing and His kingdom: \v 2 Preach the word; be prepared in season \add and\add* out of season; reprove, rebuke, \add and\add* encourage with every \add form of\add* patient instruction.
\p \v 3 For \add the\add* time will come when men will not tolerate sound doctrine, but with itching ears they will gather around themselves teachers to suit \add their\add* own desires. \v 4 \add So\add* they will turn \add their\add* ears \add away\add* from the truth and turn aside to myths.
\p \v 5 But you, be sober in all things, endure hardship, do \add the\add* work of an evangelist, fulfill your ministry. \v 6 For I \add am\add* already being poured out like a drink offering, and the time of my departure is at hand. \v 7 I have fought the good fight, I have finished the race, I have kept the faith. \v 8 From now on there is laid up for me the crown of righteousness, which the Lord, the righteous Judge, will award to me on that day — and not only to me, but to all who crave His appearing.
\s1 Personal Concerns
\p \v 9 Make every effort to come to me quickly, \v 10 because Demas, in his love of this \add world\add*, has deserted me and gone to Thessalonica. Crescens \add has gone\add* to Galatia, \add and\add* Titus to Dalmatia. \v 11 Only Luke is with me. Get Mark \add and\add* bring \add him\add* with you, because he is useful to me in \add the\add* ministry. \v 12 Tychicus, however, I have sent to Ephesus. \v 13 When you come, bring the cloak that I left with Carpus at Troas, and \add my\add* scrolls, especially the parchments.
\p \v 14 Alexander the coppersmith did great harm to me. The Lord will repay him according to his deeds. \v 15 You too should beware of \add him\add*, for he has vigorously opposed our message.
\s1 The Lord Remains Faithful
\p \v 16 At my first defense, no one stood with me, but everyone deserted me. May it not be charged against them. \v 17 But the Lord stood by me and strengthened me, so that through me the message would be fully proclaimed, and all the Gentiles would hear \add it\add*. \add So\add* I was delivered from \add the\add* mouth of the lion. \v 18 \add And\add* the Lord will rescue me from every evil action and bring \add me\add* safely into His heavenly kingdom. To Him \add be\add* the glory forever \add and\add* ever. Amen.
\s1 Final Greetings
\r (\ref Ephesians 6:21–24|EPH 6:21-24\ref*; \ref Philippians 4:21–23|PHP 4:21-23\ref*)
\p \v 19 Greet Prisca\f + \fr 4:19 \fqa Prisca \ft is a variant of \fqa Priscilla\ft ; see \ref Acts 18:2|ACT 18:2\ref*.\f* and Aquila, as well as the household of Onesiphorus.
\p \v 20 Erastus has remained at Corinth, and Trophimus I left sick in Miletus.
\p \v 21 Make every effort to come  \add to me \add* before winter.
\p Eubulus sends you greetings, as do Pudens, Linus, Claudia, and all the brothers.
\p \v 22 The Lord \add be\add* with your spirit. Grace \add be\add* with you all.\f + \fr 4:22 \ft BYZ and TR include \fqa Amen.\f*
